## Understanding the Mutation

The mutation removes a `__syncthreads()` call at line 63 in the `fused_gemm_bn_gelu_kernel`. Looking at the original code:

```cuda
for (int t = 0; t < (K + TILE_SIZE - 1) / TILE_SIZE; ++t) {
    int tiled_k = t * TILE_SIZE;

    // Load tile from input matrix A
    if (row < M && (tiled_k + threadIdx.x) < K) {
        tile_a[threadIdx.y][threadIdx.x] = input[row * K + tiled_k + threadIdx.x];
    } else {
        tile_a[threadIdx.y][threadIdx.x] = 0.0;
    }

    // Load tile from weight matrix B (transposed)
    if (col < N && (tiled_k + threadIdx.y) < K) {
        tile_b[threadIdx.y][threadIdx.x] = weight[col * K + tiled_k + threadIdx.y];
    } else {
        tile_b[threadIdx.y][threadIdx.x] = 0.0;
    }

    __syncthreads();  // <-- FIRST syncthreads (before computation)

    // Compute partial dot product
    for (int k = 0; k < TILE_SIZE; ++k) {
        acc += tile_a[threadIdx.y][k] * tile_b[k][threadIdx.x];
    }

    __syncthreads();  // <-- SECOND syncthreads (after computation, line 63 in mutant)
}
```

The mutant removes the FIRST `__syncthreads()` (not the second one at line 63). Wait, let me re-read...


Actually, looking at the mutant code, the synchronization barrier between loading tile_b and starting the dot product computation is missing. This means threads could begin reading from tile_a and tile_b before all threads have finished writing to these shared memory arrays. The computation loop starts immediately after the load operations without ensuring all threads have completed their writes.

The race condition manifests when some threads execute the dot product while others are still loading data into shared memory. Since threads within a block can execute at different rates, earlier threads might read uninitialized or partially-written values from the tiles, producing incorrect intermediate results that accumulate into the final output.

With the input dimensions of [128, 512] and TILE_SIZE of 32, the computation processes data in 16 iterations (512 / 32). Each iteration loads a 32×32 tile and computes partial dot products. The missing synchronization means this race condition could occur in every iteration, systematically corrupting the accumulated values. produce different results.

