For a concrete test, I'd use non-zero, varied values with large magnitudes to amplify differences from incorrect shared memory reads. Since the race condition occurs between threads writing to and reading from shared memory tiles, thread (0, 0) might read `tile_a[0][1]` before thread (0, 1) has finished writing it, causing stale or uninitialized data to be used in the computation.

